## 1.4.0 — 2026-09-03

pave-init 2.4.4, 2.4.5, and 2.5.0 alignment. Lead-behavior and revision-record
changes; the packaged graph's meaning does not move.

Evolution contract rule 7 is inverted. A run paused on a defect in its own
graph now continues on the reviewed, landed successor from its last satisfied
gate: the lead re-pins run state to the new revision and bundle digest, records
the authorizing approval verbatim, and landed work stays landed. A gate the
successor adds becomes a backfill duty per landed item, discharged before those
items are promoted and never marked passed for them. Closing the run and
starting a linked successor run is now the narrow exception: only a successor
that changes what a recorded outcome meant. Rule 1, resume step 1, and the
run-state schema's `workflow_identity` description now say a landing mid-run
does not move a running instance by itself, and the run-time bar reads
"never change the pinned graph's meaning in place" instead of a blanket "never
at run time". The binding-revision lane is stated as never changing graph
meaning, so never moving node, edge, or check counts, in the lead skill and the
README appendix.
  - Field evidence, this plugin's own run: it needed one review node added
    mid-run and the contract's only path was close-the-run-and-start-a-
    successor, so the v1 revision was amended in place instead.

Changed — the revision record moves from `workflow-manifest.yaml` plus full
`history/vN/` copies to one live `workflow.pave.yaml`, one append-only
`revisions.yaml`, and one `history/v<N>.patch` per landing, managed only by
`scripts/record_revision.py` (`init`, `install`, `propose`, `land`, `pin`,
`verify`, `rollback`). The package ships `revisions.yaml` (entries 0-4, patches
under `history/`) and is itself a valid root; `install` seeds a project's
evolution root from it.
`scripts/freeze_revision.py`, `codex/init_evolution_workspace.py`, and the
packaged `workflow-manifest.yaml` are removed. An existing root created by the
1.3.x manifest scheme migrates once per README "Migrating an existing
evolution root". "Freeze" is now "land".

New — `skills/vllm-neuron-parity/hooks/graph_edit_guard.sh`, registered in
`hooks/hooks.json` (PreToolUse Edit|Write|MultiEdit): denies a direct edit of a live
`*.pave.yaml` or `revisions.yaml` when `revisions.yaml` sits beside it and no
`.landing` marker exists. Eight controls register, disclosed in the skill
description.

Changed — successors are drafted and reviewed by pave-init's pave-evolve seats
(`pave-init:workflow-updater`, `pave-init:update-reviewer`), a run-time
dependency on pave-init 2.5.0 or later, disclosed in the skill's compatibility
field and the README. The lead never drafts its own successor. The Evolution
contract section shrinks from nine restated rules to one-clause applications
of rules 1, 2, 3, 6, 7, 8, and 9 with pointers to pave-init's
`references/pave-revisions.md`, records the plan fields `landing: user` and
`usage_ledger: kept`, and replaces the v1 freeze how-to with install, verify,
and pin. Run start and every resume run `record_revision.py verify
--pinned-revision --pinned-digest`: exit 3 routes per rule 7, exit 4 per
rule 9.

Changed — the run-state schema's `active_revision` minimum moves from 1 to 0,
so a ledger seeded at entry 0 pins cleanly; a fresh install pins the ledger
head.

Changed — the Claude agents `agents/adversarial-reviewer.md` and
`agents/adjudicator.md` move from opus to fable under the reviewer-tier rule (a
reviewer or adjudicator seat binds at or above the producer whose artifact it
judges). A runtime-binding change recorded by this release, user-approved
2026-09-03; the ledger holds no `kind: binding` entry because model bindings
live in `agents/*.md`, outside the YAML that `record_revision.py` lands. The
Codex binding stays gpt-5.6-sol.

Changed — lead dispatch, from the first run's corrections. The lead skill
gains a "Harness" paragraph: the package runs on Claude Code as well as Codex,
and the Codex tool names map to `Agent`, `SendMessage`, `TaskStop`, and
`ListAgents`, with pins from `agents/*.md` frontmatter; the README installs on
either harness. The stage-6 loop nodes (`scope_next_increment`,
`realize_increment`, `record_changeset`) run on one retained doer thread per
campaign instead of one thread per item (revision 4 binds it); a seat is retired in the same turn as
the state write that closes it, then the live-agent list is checked; a change
to an open seat's inputs is relayed before its result is read; internal fan-out
tiers per task (top tier for judgment, middle for medium work, low for
mechanical evidence) instead of one tier for all; a recorded gate-2 approval
stands across re-entries under the conditions the graph's
`design_approved_by_user` check states from revision 3, and the lead skill
points at that check instead of restating it. The investigator
and implementer contracts take public facts from web search or a fetch, cited
by URL. `references/artifact-layout.md` pins one `approvals/DECISIONS.md` per
campaign and one findings record per review node (a dated section per round,
one line per finding); the reviewer contract points at it.
`tests/test_workflow_pave.py` now fails when a README or newest-VERSION count
phrase disagrees with the validator, and `tests/test_codex_port.py` requires
the Claude Code tool names beside the Codex ones.
  - Field evidence, this plugin's own run: the lead spawned a seat per
